<title>USA: Schering-Plough identifies hepatitis enzyme.</title>
<headline>Schering-Plough identifies hepatitis enzyme.</headline>
<dateline>MADISON, N.J. 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Schering-Plough Corp said on Monday that scientists at its Research Institute have identified the structure of an enzyme essential to replication of the hepatitis C virus (HCV).</p>
<p>&quot;Determining the three-dimensional structure of the HCV helicase allows us to use advanced computer technology for structure-based drug design,&quot; the company said in a press release.</p>
<p>&quot;By finding a new way to target the virus, we've opened the door to the discovery of new drugs that may be more effective than anything currently available,&quot; it said.</p>
</text>
